{"v":1,"type":"session-summary","author_email":"reveries@example.com","session":"agent:fix-ci-portability","created_at":"2026-10-04T02:37:21.175Z","entries":[{"driving_event":"The evidence-import path guard added in 64bbccf could not catch its own regression: it asserted the manifest traversal with a '+'' quantifier and then resolved a hardcoded '../../../scripts/...' from the action directory. Against a manifest reverted to '../../scripts/...' the regex still matched and the hardcoded path still existed, so the suite passed on the exact bug that ships on main.","decision":"Derive the traversal count from the manifest match and resolve that same path, then require it to equal the repository-root scripts directory before stat.","impact":"The guard now fails when the manifest reverts to '../../' and when the traversal is missing, so the live 'Import fork evidence' failure and its future regression are caught by the packaging suite instead of only by CI.","recurrence_control":"scripts/actions-packaging.test.mjs resolves the manifest path exactly as the runner does and compares it to the repo root, then stats the result; verified by reverting the manifest and observing the test fail.","alternatives":["Leave the incidental-path assertion and rely on CI to notice a reverted traversal","Replace the composite action with a shell-computed absolute path outside the action directory"],"sources":[],"reveries":[],"retirements":[]}]}
